# AI handoff routing (effective 2026-09-21)

**CLAUDE IS SUSPENDED.** Do not assign Claude architecture review, engineering review, handoffs, risk/security review, production verification, coding, status requests, or any TGT / LeaseSmart work. Do not tell Troy to send anything to Claude. Do not include Claude in execution plans unless Troy explicitly restores Claude.

## Active operating model

| Role | Owner |
|------|--------|
| PM / Orchestrator | **ChatGPT** — discovery, priorities, sequencing, acceptance criteria, state consolidation, handoffs, final operational status |
| Architecture / Risk / Security | **Gemini** — architecture, dependencies, failure modes, security, assumptions. Gemini does not independently verify work it helped architect |
| Implementation / Patch Executor | **Cursor** — coding, repairs, minimal production changes, regression tests, evidence |
| Canonical ops record | **Microsoft 365 / SharePoint** |
| Independent Verifier | Separate from architect and implementer — attack-testing, production readback, final verification |
| Final approval | **Troy** |

Any old document, prompt, or rule that says “send to Claude,” “Claude review,” or “Claude architect” is superseded by this directive.

## Handoff format (when a copy block is needed)

Use **Copy for ChatGPT** (PM apply / sequencing) and/or **Copy for Gemini** (architecture / risk review). Markers:

```
--- CHATGPT HANDOFF START ---
...
--- CHATGPT HANDOFF END ---
```

```
--- GEMINI REVIEW START ---
...
--- GEMINI REVIEW END ---
```

Optional one-click copy button: same HTML pattern as before, but label must be **Copy for ChatGPT** or **Copy for Gemini** (never “Copy for Claude”).

**Handoff fields:** Project, Sprint, Build ID, Status (COMMITTED / NOT COMMITTED), What was built, Files changed, Test results, What the recipient must do next.

**Security:** Never include API keys, tokens, or secrets.

**Repo utility:** `scripts/handoff-copy-lib.mjs` may still say Claude — treat that as legacy until updated; prefer ChatGPT/Gemini labels in new reports.
